# Copy to evals/.env (gitignored) and fill in what you need.
#
# Nothing here is required to run the local benchmarks. Ollama needs no
# credential, which is the whole point of the local path being supported.
#
# A variable already set in your shell always wins over this file, so CI and
# 1Password injection keep working unchanged. Files are consulted in this order,
# first definition winning:
#
#   $OB1_ENV_FILE, evals/.env, <repo>/.env, deploy/.env
#
# Values are read literally. A trailing `# comment` is NOT stripped from an
# unquoted value — quote the value if you want one beside it.

# ── Linear ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Personal API key from https://linear.app/settings/api, for
# build-linear-corpus.ts. Read-only use; it fetches issues and comments.
#
# What it pulls is internal engineering data and stays on this machine: the
# builder refuses to write anywhere inside the repository, and the corpus never
# goes to a hosted embedding provider.
# LINEAR_API_KEY=lin_api_...

# Which team and workflow state to collect, and where to write.
# OB1_CORPUS_TEAM=SMD
# OB1_CORPUS_STATE=completed
# OB1_CORPUS_OUT=/tmp/linear-corpus-full.json
# OB1_CORPUS_COMMENTS=on

# ── Hosted model provider ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Only needed to benchmark hosted embedding or extraction models. Leave unset for
# the local Ollama path.
#
# Do NOT point a hosted provider at the Linear corpus — it is internal healthcare
# engineering data. Benchmark hosted models on synthetic input (evals/corpus.ts).
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-...
# OB1_EVAL_BASE=https://openrouter.ai/api/v1
